# Always Deploy After Changes

After any code change that affects runtime behavior or the dashboard UI, deploy to the Ubuntu AI Server before ending the turn. Do not wait for the user to ask.

## Deploy path (canonical)

Image rebuild is the source of truth. Partial `docker cp` into a running container causes revision drift.

1. **web-ui changes**: `cd web-ui && npm run build` (writes `ai-server/src/aegis_ai/web/static/ui-v2`).
2. On Ubuntu, rebuild and recreate `ai-server`:
   - `AEGIS_SOURCE_REVISION=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD) docker compose build --build-arg AEGIS_SOURCE_REVISION=$AEGIS_SOURCE_REVISION ai-server`
   - `docker compose up -d --force-recreate --no-deps ai-server`
   - or `bash scripts/ubuntu/start.sh` / `.\scripts\rebuild-ai-server.ps1`
3. Verify `/health` includes `revision`, and `docker logs aegis-ai-server-1` shows `Starting AEGIS Core (revision=...)`.
4. **Emergency only**: copy a single module with `.aegis-local/copy-ubuntu.ps1` + `docker cp`, then rebuild at the next opportunity. Do not leave a patched container as production.

## Scope

- Deploy AI Server Python + dashboard static UI for dashboard/backend changes.
- Deploy other servers (browser/pc) only when those trees changed.
- Do not commit secrets from `.aegis-local/`.
- Tell the user briefly that deploy completed (or failed with the blocker).
